RDMA/rxe: Remove unused page_offset member

jira KERNEL-1690
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-5.14.0-687.53.1.el9_8
commit-author Li Zhijian <lizhijian@fujitsu.com>
commit d3922f6dad69b3d1f7656c9035bd0e82f73091b7
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-5.14.0-687.53.1.el9_8/d3922f6d.failed

In rxe_map_mr_sg(), the `page_offset` member of the `rxe_mr` struct
was initialized based on `ibmr.iova`, which will be updated inside
ib_sg_to_pages() later.

Consequently, the value assigned to `page_offset` was incorrect. However,
since `page_offset` was never utilized throughout the code, it can be safely
removed to clean up the codebase and avoid future confusion.

	Signed-off-by: Li Zhijian <lizhijian@fujitsu.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260116032833.2574627-1-lizhijian@fujitsu.com
	Reviewed-by: Zhu Yanjun <yanjun.zhu@linux.dev>
	Signed-off-by: Leon Romanovsky <leon@kernel.org>
(cherry picked from commit d3922f6dad69b3d1f7656c9035bd0e82f73091b7)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	drivers/infiniband/sw/rxe/rxe_mr.c
#	drivers/infiniband/sw/rxe/rxe_odp.c
#	drivers/infiniband/sw/rxe/rxe_verbs.h
diff --cc drivers/infiniband/sw/rxe/rxe_mr.c
index 4a44057d38e4,05710d785a7e..000000000000
--- a/drivers/infiniband/sw/rxe/rxe_mr.c
+++ b/drivers/infiniband/sw/rxe/rxe_mr.c
@@@ -232,17 -232,13 +232,22 @@@ int rxe_map_mr_sg(struct ib_mr *ibmr, s
  		  int sg_nents, unsigned int *sg_offset)
  {
  	struct rxe_mr *mr = to_rmr(ibmr);
 -	unsigned int page_size = mr_page_size(mr);
 +	int n;
  
  	mr->nbuf = 0;
++<<<<<<< HEAD
++=======
+ 	mr->page_shift = ilog2(page_size);
+ 	mr->page_mask = ~((u64)page_size - 1);
++>>>>>>> d3922f6dad69 (RDMA/rxe: Remove unused page_offset member)
  
 -	return ib_sg_to_pages(ibmr, sgl, sg_nents, sg_offset, rxe_set_page);
 +	n = ib_sg_to_pages(ibmr, sgl, sg_nents, sg_offset, rxe_set_page);
 +
 +	mr->page_shift = ilog2(ibmr->page_size);
 +	mr->page_mask = ibmr->page_size - 1;
 +	mr->offset = ibmr->iova & mr->page_mask;
 +
 +	return n;
  }
  
  static int rxe_mr_copy_xarray(struct rxe_mr *mr, u64 iova, void *addr,
diff --cc drivers/infiniband/sw/rxe/rxe_verbs.h
index f1424d315acd,f94ce85eb807..000000000000
--- a/drivers/infiniband/sw/rxe/rxe_verbs.h
+++ b/drivers/infiniband/sw/rxe/rxe_verbs.h
@@@ -309,7 -347,6 +309,10 @@@ struct rxe_mr 
  	int			access;
  	atomic_t		num_mw;
  
++<<<<<<< HEAD
 +	u32			offset;
++=======
++>>>>>>> d3922f6dad69 (RDMA/rxe: Remove unused page_offset member)
  	unsigned int		page_shift;
  	u64			page_mask;
  
